# The build context is the repository root so the Dockerfile can reach the
# plugin tree that `scripts/stage-plow-chat-plugin.sh` stages into
# `plugins/plow_chat/` right before the build. That also puts local build
# droppings in scope — `__pycache__` appears there the moment anything imports
# the plugin, and it would otherwise be baked into an image every tenant runs.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `__pycache__/` matches only the context root,
# so the one that actually appears — under `plugins/plow_chat/` — shipped.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.git/
.github/
README.md
